---
description: Python style for claims-copilot source and tests
globs: "**/*.py"
alwaysApply: false
---

- Python 3.12, `from __future__ import annotations`, full type hints; code must pass `mypy --strict`.
- Ruff rules in `pyproject.toml` are authoritative (line length 100, `S` security rules on). Fix
  findings; use `# noqa` only with a reason on the same line.
- Records are frozen dataclasses. Use `pathlib`, `httpx`, `Decimal` for money. No floats for USD.
- Library modules do not `print`; CLIs (`__main__`, `main()`) may.
- Read paths from `claims_copilot.project`; never hard-code `PRODUCT_NAME` or repo paths.
- Prefer small pure functions with the I/O at the edges so they can be tested without the network.
- Never call a paid API directly; see the cost rule.
